MID_LGV_1LED_c07_Moo_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1LED_c07_Moo_m01_001: From what Sirocco said, {SetColor=Gold}{DateTime=Month} {DateTime=Day}{SetColor=Default} is when we\nshould go and hit the ghost carriage.
MID_LGV_1LED_c07_Moo_m01_002: We've still got time to get everything ready!\nBut make sure to find me when the day comes.
MID_LGA_1LED_c07_Moo_m01: <BLN>Are you ready?
MID_LGV_1LED_c07_Moo_m03: <TH>
MID_LGV_1LED_c07_Moo_m03_001: Sirocco said that today's the day we have to go and\nambush the ghost carriage.
MID_LGV_1LED_c07_Moo_m03_002: Are you ready to head out? Tell me when you are.
MID_LGA_1LED_c07_Moo_m03: <BLN>Gotta go today.
MID_LGV_1LED_c07_Buc_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1LED_c07_Buc_m01_001: It felt bittersweet, seeing you engaging in happy\nchitchat with others your age in that match.
MID_LGV_1LED_c07_Buc_m01_002: I could not help but remember how badly I wanted\nyou to walk in the sun.
MID_LGV_1LED_c07_Buc_m01_003: If not for what happened to us, I'm sure by now you\nwould have grown into a happy young woman.
MID_LGV_1LED_c07_Buc_m01_004: Even if it must be after you get your revenge, I want\nto see you reach that future.
MID_LGV_1LED_c07_Buc_m01_005: I will expend every effort to help you get there.
MID_LGA_1LED_c07_Buc_m01: <BLN>It was bittersweet.
MID_LGV_1LED_c07_Sci_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1LED_c07_Sci_m01_001: It's difficult to say whether our plan will be\nsuccessful or if we'll just poke the hornet's nest.
MID_LGV_1LED_c07_Sci_m01_002: In either case I daresay we will uncover the truth\nbehind the ghost carriage and its cargo.
MID_LGV_1LED_c07_Sci_m01_003: Though of course, that won't be of much use if they\nkill us in retaliation.
MID_LGA_1LED_c07_Sci_m01: <BLN>What will we discover?
MID_LGV_1LED_c07_Moo_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_1LED_c07_Moo_m02_001: Something you and Queen Theodora have in\ncommon is you're both reaaally pretty.
MID_LGV_1LED_c07_Moo_m02_002: But it was weird... After the match, it seemed like\nshe didn't hear what her allies were saying.
MID_LGV_1LED_c07_Moo_m02_003: That gave me the creeps. Eugh! You're going to be\nOK though, right?
MID_LGV_1LED_c07_Moo_m02_004: I never want to see you like that.
MID_LGV_1LED_c07_Oly_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1LED_c07_Oly_m01_001: I have been asked to compose a song for an\nupcoming event at the temple.
MID_LGV_1LED_c07_Oly_m01_002: Ohoho. Soon you shall see, Leilidahna!
MID_LGV_1LED_c07_Oly_m01_003: I will create a masterpiece wholly worthy of my\nlofty title as the Blue Rose of Caelus...
MID_LGV_1LED_c07_Oly_m01_004: and every time it rings in your ears, you will feel\nthe sting of defeat!
MID_LGA_1LED_c07_Oly_m01: <BLN>You shall see!
MID_LGV_1LED_c07_Car_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1LED_c07_Car_m01_001: Leilidahna, I hope Syracusio is making\nhimself useful.
MID_LGV_1LED_c07_Car_m01_002: There's no doubt that the man is capable, but he\ntends to go too far with his scheming.
MID_LGV_1LED_c07_Car_m01_003: Though I'll grant that he does it with the best of\nintentions.
MID_LGV_1LED_c07_Car_m01_004: If you do have any concerns about him, come and\ndiscuss them with me at once.
MID_LGA_1LED_c07_Car_m01: <BLN>Is Syracusio availing you?
MID_LGV_1LED_c07_B01_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1LED_c07_B01_m01_001: Father Mahdel was a high priest here in Dagsion\nuntil 1441.
MID_LGV_1LED_c07_B01_m01_002: But at a certain point, there was a bit of an incident\nat Dagda's temple.
MID_LGV_1LED_c07_B01_m01_003: It was a scandal that could have turned into a\nmajor blowup.
MID_LGV_1LED_c07_B01_m01_004: Though seemingly, it all grew out of a minor quarrel\nbetween priests.
MID_LGV_1LED_c07_B01_m01_005: Father Mahdel took full responsibility for the incident\nand resigned from his position.
MID_LGA_1LED_c07_B01_m01: <BLN>Father Mahdel took responsibility.
MID_LGV_1LED_c07_B02_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1LED_c07_B02_m01_001: Father Mahdel always lived alone, with no one he\ncalled family.
MID_LGV_1LED_c07_B02_m01_002: I hear the house he used to live in was torn down\nlong since.
MID_LGA_1LED_c07_B02_m01: <BLN>No family in the world.
MID_LGV_1LED_c07_B03_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1LED_c07_B03_m01_001: Father Mahdel had a best friend back in the day.\nGuillermo, who was a praetor at the time.
MID_LGV_1LED_c07_B03_m01_002: There's a rumor that they were competing for the\naffections of a woman named Hilaria.
MID_LGV_1LED_c07_B03_m01_003: Personally, I'm inclined to believe it. I once caught\nthe two of them having a fierce argument.
MID_LGA_1LED_c07_B03_m01: <BLN>His best friend.
MID_LGV_1LED_c07_B04_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1LED_c07_B04_m01_001: When Guillermo took up the role of viceroy, leaving\nDagsion to lead Cydonia...
MID_LGV_1LED_c07_B04_m01_002: Hilaria chose to go with him.
MID_LGV_1LED_c07_B04_m01_003: Father Mahdel was stewing about that for a long,\nlong time afterward.
MID_LGA_1LED_c07_B04_m01: <BLN>The man held a grudge.
MID_LGV_1LED_c07_B05_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1LED_c07_B05_m01_001: Mahdel? I haven't heard that name in a long time.\nYou mean the high priest of Dagda's temple, right?
MID_LGV_1LED_c07_B05_m01_002: From all I heard he was an upstanding man—\nsomeone highly trusted by the Divine Sovereign.
MID_LGA_1LED_c07_B05_m01: <BLN>Mahdel?
MID_LGV_1LED_c07_B06_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1LED_c07_B06_m01_001: It's said Hilaria had a frail constitution.
MID_LGV_1LED_c07_B06_m01_002: If you believe the rumors, Father Mahdel was\ntirelessly researching ways to extend the lifespan...
MID_LGV_1LED_c07_B06_m01_003: Maybe he was doing it for her.
MID_LGA_1LED_c07_B06_m01: <BLN>His research...